{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat","id":1361244,"title":"Wrights: Architects of Soul and Will (Minor Splat)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-16T02:22:19-08:00","id":1361244,"title":"Wrights: Architects of Soul and Will (Minor Splat)","content":"So, I started this around mid-November, and it's finally gotten to a point where I both like it and think the lawyers won't chase me - so here you are. Discussion, commentary and criticism are all more than welcome:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MtSY-TFMlbRO3ZF736k4tw48COBLchq3ZadIhLbKMNs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MtSY-TFMlbRO3ZF736k4tw48COBLchq3ZadIhLbKMNs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MtSY-TFMlbRO3ZF736k4tw48COBLchq3ZadIhLbKMNs/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1MtSY-TFMlbRO3ZF736k4tw48COBLchq3ZadIhLbKMNs/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T09:21:22-08:00","id":1361285,"title":"","content":"Everything about this is awesome. THIS is basically the Mummy character template I want. This looks fantastic. <br /> <br /> There are two things I would want to add, both rate to the same thing, time. I would find a way to make them immortal and find a way to let them jump through time, as I like that element from the second edition. <br /> <br /> Oh, and I might find another way besides sacrifice to raise Sekhem. <br /> <br /> But yeah, this is brilliant. Its a great structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T09:43:13-08:00","id":1361290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361285#post1361285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everything about this is awesome. THIS is basically the Mummy character template I want. This looks fantastic.<br /> <br /> There are two things I would want to add, both rate to the same thing, time. I would find a way to make them immortal and find a way to let them jump through time, as I like that element from the second edition.</div> </div> </div> </div> One of the central elements of Wrights is that if they want stuff, they have to work for it. I think you'll find I included two methods of immortality in the thing - the Rites of Dancing with the Dusk and Rising with the Sun, and Keshina. And... well, I suspect it's just a matter of differing opinions, but I really, <i>really</i> don't like the way 2e Mummy does the time travel thing. Though, I could certainly adapt the Utterance of he Disciples of the Wheel (from <i>Sothis Ascends</i>) to 2e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361285#post1361285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I might find another way besides sacrifice to raise Sekhem.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can raise Sekhem by sacrificing Vessels, and via Talismans and Keshina - those are <i>very</i> important for Wrights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T10:23:08-08:00","id":1361295,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of gaining power abilities slowly, piecemeal. Its fun. At first such a character is only barely more then human but given time, and the experiences of adventure, they become more. <br /> <br /> I also really like the Rites of Dancing with the Dusk and Rising with the Sun. The idea one makes them super old and then tje next toung again, well, its awesome. I do think a year is too short, and I also see no benfot in the risk - im pretty sure I wouldnt end a gme cayse a player's character dies due to a bad roll in his home. BUT, that said, I like the idea. <br /> <br /> (Honestly, I think my issue with the roll thing is Im not really a fan of the way Rites are designed. At least not when supernaturals perfprm them.) <br /> <br /> On the time travel thing, that's fine. Honestly, its easy to add in - add a Rite - when its wanted. <br /> <br /> Your Vessel notes, plus talisman, is cool. I like the nature. <br /> <br /> On Sekhem, I guess I am just a fan of exprience being used to boost it, not beeaking other things. But I can see the fun in your way. <br /> <br /> I should add that at first glance I wasn't a fan of burning sekhem dot to power an Utterance. But, upon thibking, thematically its nifty. The power isnt easy and natural and so a Wright meeds to fuel it potently. Its cool. It aso makes all the sense as Utterances are late session, boss fight powers, not &quot;i walk into a room and cast an Utterance just because!&quot; power. <br /> <br /> The Wights having Sekhem 1 to 10 is perfect (I hate the other progression.) The Merits they have are very cool. I also love there access to Pillars, Affinities, and Utterances. That and Vessels aa well. <br /> <br /> Oh, as a wuestion, and maybe I missed it, but Wrights can buy new Affinities with experience. Right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T10:25:18-08:00","id":1361296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361295#post1361295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, as a wuestion, and maybe I missed it, but Wrights can buy new Affinities with experience. Right?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep. In the contents section, you'll find 'Experience Costs'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:10:33-08:00","id":1361304,"title":"","content":"Regarding the two Rites, the idea is very much that they're a... stopgap measure, so to speak. They're basically a less abhorrent version of Blood Bather immortality. I do agree with you re: the 'bad roll' issue, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:31:00-08:00","id":1361310,"title":"","content":"Longevity. Those two rites being a stepping stone is great. Maybe a followu Rite could exist that rewuires a Vessel and boosts them to decades or something. This cpuld be a stuff of campaign story rather then something else. <br /> <br /> Rites. The whole only one Pillar can be used to modify a Rite is not something I'm a fan of. I think I might add amerit that allows for multiple Pillars to be used to change a rite. Maybe call it Sorcerous Shaping and have a 2-dot and 4-dot version, each adds +1 to pillars points used while increasing certain Sekhem and pillar dot requirements. <br /> <br /> Just read your Affinities doc. YES!!!!! These are awesome. Honestly, this is exactly what I wanted. Sooo many nifty ideas as I read through it. <br /> <br /> On Utterances. I like how you mention some visuals can change but that what they inherently are should stay. Thats great. <br /> <br /> As a random question, have you thought of societies for them. I could see the Wrights forming a fellowship based on a common nature. <br /> <br /> So much fun to be had here. <br /> <br /> (Ps. Using my phone, hence the typing errors. Just sayin! Hehe)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-16T11:47:17-08:00","id":1361315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361310#post1361310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longevity. Those two rites being a stepping stone is great. Maybe a followu Rite could exist that rewuires a Vessel and boosts them to decades or something. This cpuld be a stuff of campaign story rather then something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Enduring Flesh Affinity adds (Ka) decades of healthy life to the Wright's allotted span.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361310#post1361310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rites. The whole only one Pillar can be used to modify a Rite is not something I'm a fan of. I think I might add amerit that allows for multiple Pillars to be used to change a rite. Maybe call it Sorcerous Shaping and have a 2-dot and 4-dot version, each adds +1 to pillars points used while increasing certain Sekhem and pillar dot requirements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I ahve to admit I have mixed feelings on that. I could see something like that working, but I'd probably require a not-Descent roll as if you were unleashing a Tier 1 Utterance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361310#post1361310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random question, have you thought of societies for them. I could see the Wrights forming a fellowship based on a common nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm not very good at the societies side of things. I do have a section marked out for that (you may notice 'Building Societies' in the main document; no I won't apologize for the pun), but I haven't really done anything in there yet. Part of it is that I think Wrights should be pretty rare.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:30:35-08:00","id":1361459,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> , what is it you dislike about only being able to ameliorate one element of a Rite via Pillars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T07:59:23-08:00","id":1361468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361459#post1361459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> , what is it you dislike about only being able to ameliorate one element of a Rite via Pillars?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think if you are basically a supernatural being with high magic on your own you should be able to conduct magic without using the crutches of mundane folk. You don't need time or place or object, your sheer overwhelming power lets your will conduct the magic. To me this is both practically and thematically important when the suprnatural has powers that are intrinsically greater than mundane rites. <br /> <br /> I'm also a fan of adding supernatural potency to all mundane magic using rolls to represent your greater knowledge of arcane truths when casting magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:10:51-08:00","id":1361471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361468#post1361468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I think if you are basically a supernatural being with high magic on your own you should be able to conduct magic without using the crutches of mundane folk. You don't need time or place or object, your sheer overwhelming power lets your will conduct the magic. To me this is both practically and thematically important when the suprnatural has powers that are intrinsically greater than mundane rites.<br /> <br /> I'm also a fan of adding supernatural potency to all mundane magic using rolls to represent your greater knowledge of arcane truths when casting magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, I honestly disagree with that. I'll point out mages' use of yantras, Werewolf rites, vampiric blood sorcery and so on as well. And, as you say, Wrights already have access to Utterances - the advantage of Rites is that they're malleable: <i>you can create new ones</i>. And, well, they're <i>Rites; </i>rituals<i>. </i><br /> <br /> So, in short, I could see a Merit which allows you to spend two Pillar points on a single Rite, but not all three elements - a 'three options, pick two' situation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:22:08-08:00","id":1361476,"title":"","content":"Roght, but see te thing about &quot;mages' use of yantras, Werewolf rites, vampiric blood sorcery&quot; is that they are group specific. They are calibrated around the power source of said template. <br /> <br /> Sorcery Rites are mortal magics. They are lesser things compared to what other beings can do. Which is why in this case the Wrights, or the Reborn for example, overwhelming power should allow them to ignore aome trappings.<br /> <br /> All that said. I can see letting Wrights replace one element with a Pillar naturally. I could see a merit and sekhem under 5 letting a second element be reduced. Now that would be all fpr most BUT I could see a second merit at 3 dkts and Sekhem 6+ allowing the replacement of all three elements. At this point you are a potent bein and there should be an advantage. <br /> <br /> As a note, I'm not a fan of the Resolve and Occult maximums on Rites either. I say even mortals should get some based on that and others based on slots purchased by experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:28:19-08:00","id":1361477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361476#post1361476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said. I can see letting Wrights replace one element with a Pillar naturally. I could see a merit and sekhem under 5 letting a second element be reduced. Now that would be all fpr most BUT I could see a second merit at 3 dkts and Sekhem 6+ allowing the replacement of all three elements. At this point you are a potent bein and there should be an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that, potentially.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361476#post1361476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, I'm not a fan of the Resolve and Occult maximums on Rites either. I say even mortals should get some based on that and others based on slots purchased by experience.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>points at the Sorcerous Knowledge Merit</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:35:26-08:00","id":1361481,"title":"","content":"The cool thing about merits is its easy to add. Hehe<br /> <br /> Also, for the record, your awesome Sorcerous Knowledge merit is different from the one in 2e curse. That one has a Resolve maximum, yours don't. I like yours, and would ignore their max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T08:41:56-08:00","id":1361482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361481#post1361481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The cool thing about merits is its easy to add. Hehe<br /> <br /> Also, for the record, your awesome Sorcerous Knowledge merit is different from the one in 2e curse. That one has a Resolve maximum, yours don't. I like yours, and would ignore their max.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was why I changed it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I might make my version Wrights-only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T09:11:31-08:00","id":1361491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361482#post1361482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was why I changed it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Though I might make my version Wrights-only.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hehe. Cool. <br /> <br /> Yeah, small restrictions like that make no sense to me. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see a point in making it Wright only. Especially as I ckuld see ypur version being used for lesser immortals like the reborn as well. <br /> <br /> I really do have to say your character type sounds perfect to me. Its basically what I want out of Mummy. Sekhem 1 to 10. Access to Pillars, Affinities, Utterances. Cool fun Merits and Sorcerous Rites. Its very much a good way to do it. <br /> <br /> I definetly woud include, and you do mention it, Cult access. Mostly bevause leading others is very much in theme for the powers available very much fit that. <br /> <br /> Also, considering how Wright is a crafter title, I could still see Guild being applied to the society. That or Lodge. Hehe","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T09:33:26-08:00","id":1361499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361491#post1361491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hehe. Cool.<br /> <br /> Yeah, small restrictions like that make no sense to me.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see a point in making it Wright only. Especially as I ckuld see ypur version being used for lesser immortals like the reborn as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see your point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361491#post1361491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do have to say your character type sounds perfect to me. Its basically what I want out of Mummy. Sekhem 1 to 10. Access to Pillars, Affinities, Utterances. Cool fun Merits and Sorcerous Rites. Its very much a good way to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do <i>like</i> Mummy, but honestly... there's the pacing issues the Descent and - more specifically - death at the end of it introduces, as well as the fact that, well, it's a very... specialist game. It's kinda hard to convince people to play it.<br /> <br /> Thematically, Wrights are figures like Moses or Myrddin - mighty sorcerers in potential, with subtler powers and potencies they can access more often. Amusingly, they're a rather good fit for Gandalf, what with his quiet power most of the time, and then occasionally going all YOU SHALL NOT PASS! And yes, I know Gandalf is basically an incarnated not!angel, but that's beside the point.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361491#post1361491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definetly woud include, and you do mention it, Cult access. Mostly bevause leading others is very much in theme for the powers available very much fit that.<br /> <br /> Also, considering how Wright is a crafter title, I could still see Guild being applied to the society. That or Lodge. Hehe</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should mention Cult access, as I'm currently playtesting cults in a non-Mummy game (specifically a Mage/Demon crossover). I'll PM you the stuff about it, as it's basically just 2e Mummy cults - the system seems surprisingly robust and versatile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-17-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T12:24:49-08:00","id":1361540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361499#post1361499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thematically, Wrights are figures like Moses or Myrddin - mighty sorcerers in potential, with subtler powers and potencies they can access more often. Amusingly, they're a rather good fit for Gandalf, what with his quiet power most of the time, and then occasionally going all YOU SHALL NOT PASS! And yes, I know Gandalf is basically an incarnated not!angel, but that's beside the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh. I love this. This is a sort of thematic idea I adore. Its also honestly why I love the Pillar plus Affinity plus Utterance system. It lets usdo such things. <br /> <br /> So yeah, I love said inspiration. I live tge idea quite a lot actually. <br /> <br /> When it comes to mummy I am too much a fan of Resurrection to be entirely happy with the direction they took Curse. For all that I own all 1e books. 2e Curse, minus Sekhem, is really good for me, with it having a lot of fun potential. <br /> <br /> I do really like the Reborn, though they lack Affinities which Wrights do. <br /> <br /> +++ <br /> <br /> I do have one thematic and mechanical question for you. I'm interested in hearing why you choose to remove raising Sekhem with experience and made it based on sacrifice, Vessel or person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T13:41:25-08:00","id":1361554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361540#post1361540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have one thematic and mechanical question for you. I'm interested in hearing why you choose to remove raising Sekhem with experience and made it based on sacrifice, Vessel or person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Three main reasons:<br /> <br /> One, because the previous version I tried with a 'permanent' power splat (it was called Puissance) felt like it didn't have any 'catch' or 'issue'. Mages have Obsessions, werewolves have their rage, Prometheans have being a Promethean, but Wrights just... had powers.<br /> <br /> Two, one of the central themes of <i>Mummy</i> is a choice between power and slavery, or freedom and weakness. I decided to take this and tweak it a little with Wrights, such that if you want to be powerful you need to accept one of two strictures: either husband your power carefully, using it only when you really need to, or face the issue of upkeep.<br /> <br /> Three, Wrights are thematically based around building themselves up, so it made sense to me to gamify that aspect of them; spending XP on a power stat isn't a very interesting thing, but having to choose between unleashing your full might and being safer (via Supernatural Tolerance) makes for an interesting dynamic, I think, as does the fact that the very way Sekhem functions asks both Wright and player the question &quot;What are you willing to do for power?&quot; Are you willing to sacrifice a few people to gain the power to banish that monster with a meteor? Are you willing to sacrifice your magical panoply? Is the short-term gain worth the long-term loss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T15:30:47-08:00","id":1361585,"title":"","content":"One thing I have been considering is whether it would be alright to create an Affinity for 'works of idea' (e.g. written stuff) as a kind of counterpart to Hand of the Maker, to let you do things like decipher or create codes/subtle meanings or to do so with superhuman speed and skill, or whether that would be too close to a Sesha-Hebsu thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T17:50:40-08:00","id":1361619,"title":"","content":"O<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361585#post1361585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I have been considering is whether it would be alright to create an Affinity for 'works of idea' (e.g. written stuff) as a kind of counterpart to Hand of the Maker, to let you do things like decipher or create codes/subtle meanings or to do so with superhuman speed and skill, or whether that would be too close to a Sesha-Hebsu thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think an Affinity that enhances writing, research, discovery, interpretation, and analysis and other such 'works of idea' as you say makes perfect sense. Being the scribe and or the vizier is just as important and useful as being the crafter or the general. So yeah, Affinities that enhance such things are brilliant. <br /> <br /> Plus, I think there is something awesome about a mummy / Wright having the ability to make or design or organize the creation of works of whatever much quicker than others is brilliant to me.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> On the topic of Sekhem, thanks for that info. While I don't really like said limitation I understand where you are coming from with it. (Though I have to admit I would probably find a way to make either Vessels easier to get, maybe as part of plot adventure hooks, or add an experience cost to raising Sekhem.)<br /> <br /> I also have to note I am not entirely a fan of the permanent use of Sekhem to power Utterances. I think maybe a way to solve this in a way that I find enjoyable is that you loose the Skhem dot temporarily, maybe for the adventure, but that it comes back next adventure. That way there is still a limitation, but its not unfun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T02:14:42-08:00","id":1361690,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that Wrights can actually make Vestiges and Vessels. Both of those are Open Rites, and unlike mummies Wrights have the soul to perform such things. Plus, with a Talisman or Keshina Wrights can get 'free' Sekhem to create said Vessels without having to murder people or break other Vessels. Plus, Wrights have access to the Fivefold Compass to lead them to Vessels, and were I running a Wright game I'd certainly make Vessels a part of the plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-18-2020, 05:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T07:28:31-08:00","id":1361728,"title":"","content":"Regarding power stat gain: what about constructing monuments to refine and channel the Sekhem to the Wright? The more they grow in might, the more they are tied down to protecting the base of that power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T07:46:46-08:00","id":1361730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1361728#post1361728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding power stat gain: what about constructing monuments to refine and channel the Sekhem to the Wright? The more they grow in might, the more they are tied down to protecting the base of that power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some kind of advanced Geometry? I could see that. Though Enshrined Glory kind-of does that already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 01-18-2020, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T04:16:11-07:00","id":1376389,"title":"","content":"This might be considered necromancy but I just wanted to say this template with a little re-skinning could be a great way to play a wuxia or xianxia style game. What do you think? I dont know exactly how I would go about it but it seems like a cool idea. Maybe the different soul parts would be daos or something any way really neat stuff thanks for writing it up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T03:55:45-07:00","id":1376504,"title":"","content":"Skimmed through and I dig it. Waiting for the final version of Mummy 2nd ed before I read it, but it mentions Utterances to level 5, did 2nd ed change things and Utterances are no longer 1-3 in level?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:36:51-07:00","id":1376510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1376504#post1376504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skimmed through and I dig it. Waiting for the final version of Mummy 2nd ed before I read it, but it mentions Utterances to level 5, did 2nd ed change things and Utterances are no longer 1-3 in level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each Utterance still has three Tiers, but each Tier has a Pillar requirement that ranges from 1-5 depending on Utterance and Tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-25T04:41:55-07:00","id":1376513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1376510#post1376510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Each Utterance still has three Tiers, but each Tier has a Pillar requirement that ranges from 1-5 depending on Utterance and Tier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahh thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T03:36:53-07:00","id":1376694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hyperspacewizard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1361244-wrights-architects-of-soul-and-will-minor-splat?p=1376389#post1376389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This might be considered necromancy but I just wanted to say this template with a little re-skinning could be a great way to play a wuxia or xianxia style game. What do you think? I dont know exactly how I would go about it but it seems like a cool idea. Maybe the different soul parts would be daos or something any way really neat stuff thanks for writing it up</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually made a start on that, swapping out the soul-parts for elements (wood, metal, earth, water, fire).<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wuxia</span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Changes:</span></span><ul><li>Replace \u2018Wright\u2019 with \u2018Fangshi\u2019</li> <li>Replace \u2018Sekhem\u2019 with \u2018Qi\u2019.</li> <li>Replace \u2018Pillars\u2019 with \u2018Elements\u2019</li> <li>Replace \u2018Pillar Point(s)\u2019 with \u2018[Elemental] Breath\u2019 (e.g. Fire Breath, Metal Breath etc)</li> <li>Replace the descriptions of the Pillars with the following:</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fangshi differ from ordinary residents of the Middle Kingdom in that they have cultivated a mystical connection to the five elements which compose all things. This applies not only to the physical representations of those elements, but to the spiritual principles they represent. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Determine your defining Element based on what best fits the core of your identity and personality. You can distribute effective Element dots equal to your Willpower among the five Elements, allocating new dots whenever your permanent Willpower increases, and choosing which become dormant whenever your Willpower falls. No other Element can be rated higher than you defining Element at any time. Only one Element may have no dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Elements are as follows:</span></span><ul><li>Fire: The element of Fire represents the emotional and social domains of reality; words burn in the minds of those who hear them, and rebellion spreads like wildfire across the land. Those defined by Fire heart are loving and beloved, a radiant presence who cannot help but live according to the dictates of passion. Among Fansghi, they are sometimes called the Ardent.<ul><li>A Fangshi defined by Fire gains the following abilities:<ul><li>The character regains one Breath point of their choice after any scene in which they are able to revel in victory over a rival, or overcome challenges by appealing to others\u2019 emotions or through improvisation.</li> <li>Once per chapter, the Ardent may fully restore their Fire Breath through an intense emotional experience, provided the event seems novel to them.</li> <li>When the Fangshi improves a character\u2019s impression of her during Social Maneuvering, she learns one of that character\u2019s Aspirations, feeling his desires like the warmth of a flame upon her flesh.</li> <li>All flames are alike, and so the Fangshi may take into herself the emotions of others. Spend a Breath point while touching another character to make a (Resolve + Empathy) roll. If successful, choose an emotion-based Condition affecting the target. The character loses the Condition without resolving it, and the Fangshi gains the Condition.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Wood: Fire consumes forests, floods drown grasslands and typhoons flatten trees - and yet, life arises once more with near-infinite vitality. This is the truth of Wood:to live is to grow. Those defined by Wood are tireless idealists, forever seeking the future and whatever it may bring. They thrive on challenge and adversity, only growing stronger in response to difficulty.<ul><li>A Fangshi defined by Wood gains the following abilities:<ul><li>The Fangshi regains one Breath of her choice after any scene in which she chooses to mentally or physically challenge herself. The challenge must contain some risk of failure, but she regains the Breath point even if she fails.</li> <li>Once per chapter, the Fangshi\u2019s Wood Breath may be fully restored by learning or creating something unique, new or novel, whether a technique, a house or a weapon.</li> <li>Once per chapter per dot of Wood, the Fangshi may gain the Inspired Condition when she makes a contested action against an enemy, regardless of whether she fails or succeeds.</li> <li>When helping another character fulfill an Aspiration, the Fangshi achieves an exceptional success on rolls with three success.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Metal: Metal is the element of civilization, determination, rigidity, persistence and strength. Fangshi who define themselves with metal align themselves with these ideals; they are stubborn, tough and often quick to take the simplest and most direct route to a goal.<ul><li>A Fangshi attuned to Metal gains the following abilities:<ul><li>After any scene in which the Fangshi overcomes a challenge by tearing away extraneous details and breaking the issue down to its basic essence, they regain one Breath of their choosing.</li> <li>Once per chapter, the Fangshi\u2019s Metal Breath may be fully restored by triumphing over a challenge that entails severe consequences if she fails.</li> <li>When the Fangshi successfully opens Doors during Social Maneuvering using intimidation or violence, she gains the Steadfast Condition.</li> <li>The Fangshi benefits from 1/0 armor, which stacks with any other armor she possesses.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Water: Water is the binding essence of the world; it flows in its veins, encircles it in the ocean and falls from the heavens as rain. It is the element of wisdom, wit, flexibility and connection, for it unifies all living things. Nevertheless, when it flows in power it is among the most terrifying of the elements.<ul><li>A Fangshi defined by Water gains the following abilities:<ul><li>The Fangshi regains one Breath point of her choice after any scene in which she overcomes a serious problem by devising an unconventional solution or otherwise taking the path of least resistance.</li> <li>Once per chapter, the Fangshi may fully restore her Water Element by making common cause with an erstwhile enemy or by persuading others to do the same with one another.</li> <li>When engaging in Social Maneuvering, if the Fangshi\u2019s goal would be a breaking point for the character she is trying to influence, add one Door instead of two.</li> <li>When the Fangshi improves a character\u2019s impression of her during Social Maneuvering, she gains the Informed Condition regarding that character.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Earth: When hope falls into darkness, passion is met with denial and ambition with failure, it is the earth that endures. Earth represents not only the physical earth, but also the spiritual side of existence - all things are part of the earth, and will return to it in time. Those Fangshi who define themselves by the Earth have a special connection with both natural spirits and the spirits of the dead.<ul><li>A Fangshi defined by Earth gains the following abilities:<ul><li>She regains one Breath of her choice after any scene in which her wisdom helps another character confront their fears, or in which she shows no fear in the face of possible destruction.</li> <li>Once per chapter, the Fangshi may fully restore her Earth Breath by bringing peace, accord or resolution to the living and the dead.</li> <li>She may spend a point of Breath to make a (Composure + Occult) roll. On a success, her spirit leaves her body, gaining the Disembodied Condition. Touching her body again resolves the Condition. If something destroys the Fangshi\u2019s body while she still possesses the Disembodied Condition, she immediately dies and leaves a ghost of Rank equal to (Defining Element - 1), minimum 1.</li> <li>When touching an object or person, the Wright knows if it is a ghost\u2019s anchor.</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><ul><li>Replace \u2018seba\u2019 with \u2018zhouyu\u2019.</li> <li>Replace \u2018Keshina\u2019 with \u2018Yuanying\u2019.</li> <li>Replace \u2018Sybaris\u2019 with \u2018\u2019.</li> <li>Replace \u2018Seal the Flesh\u2019 with \u2018Vital Breath\u2019.</li> <li>Replace \u2018Arising in Might\u2019 with \u2018Elemental Prowess\u2019<ul><li>Elemental Prowess may be used to increase the following Attributes based on defining Element:<ul><li>Fire: Presence</li> <li>Wood: Intelligence</li> <li>Metal: Resolve</li> <li>Water: Wits</li> <li>Earth: Composure</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>Companions who benefit from the Fangshi\u2019s Rite of the Faithful Heart gain the following benefits based on Elements:<ul><li>Burning Spirit: A Companion whose master has Fire 5 gains +2 dice to resist or overpower a character who attempts to sway him servant from his master. The Companion may give his master any Willpower he recovers from fulfilling his Virtue or Vice, instead of gaining the benefit himself.</li> <li>Verdant Self: A Companion whose master has Wood 5 heals at twice the normal rate. When acting as a secondary actor in a teamwork action supporting his master, he adds 2 dice to his pool and negates the effect of any Dramatic Failure by himself or other secondary actors upon the Fangshi\u2019s pool.</li> <li>Perfected Body: A Companion whose master has Metal 5 may exchange up to 4 bashing wounds or 2 lethal wounds to or from his master, with permission from the Fangshi, as a Reflexive action. The Companion cannot accept further wounds if he has any aggravated wounds. This power is effective irrespective of distance.</li> <li>Flowing Mind: A Companion whose master has Water 5 shares a true telepathic bond with his master and can mentally communicate in whole sentences with her. The Companion cannot communicate in this way if he has suffered any aggravated wounds. This power is effective irrespective of distance.</li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Harmonic Soul:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> A Companion whose master has Earth 5 exists in harmony with creation, gaining 2 dice to Clash of Wills rolls, whether resisting or attacking.</span></span></li> </ul></li> </ul></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 03-26-2020, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T04:40:41-07:00","id":1376696,"title":"","content":"Yeah it surprisingly works really well. I could see using the rules for rituals or even taking some ideals from geist 2e ceremonies to make pills or formations. Spirit animals could be animals that grow up around some place where chi or sekhem is in high concentration and could gain souls pillars and be able to think. Spirit weapons I dont know what rules to pull from to really capture that feel though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11277-hyperspacewizard","name":"hyperspacewizard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-26T06:29:28-07:00","id":1376701,"title":"","content":"<d